# Responsive UI / UX

Every UI change and feature must work well on phone (~375px) and desktop. Prefer useful clarity over decorative chrome.

## Shell (ops app)

- **`md+`:** collapsible sidebar (`AppNav`)
- **`< md`:** bottom tabs (primary destinations) + **More** sheet — do not invent per-page nav
- Keep gym-floor actions (check-in, members, classes) in primary tabs when the role allows
- Respect bottom-bar clearance and `safe-area-inset-*` on fixed chrome

## Layout

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — desktop-only density
<div className="grid grid-cols-4 gap-6 p-8">

// ✅ GOOD — stack first, expand later
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 p-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 lg:gap-6 lg:p-8">
```

- Touch targets ≥ ~44px
- Avoid `min-w-[36rem]` tables without a mobile alternative (cards / stack / intentional scroll)
- One job per section; no competing chrome

## Design system

- Reuse `--color-*`, shared `Input` / `Button` / `Dialog` / form fields
- No one-off visual forks or hardcoded product copy — `es` + `en` dictionaries
- Icon-only controls need `aria-label`; nav links use `aria-current` when active

